<style data-path="/content/nexus/en/newsroom/press-releases/2026/wipro-announces-results-for-the-quarter-ended-september-30-2026/jcr:content/root/container/container/container/separator" nonce="MTc5MjA5NTg2ODMzMjAuMzMyNjI1OTM=">.cmp-separator--205847742 {height:40px;}</style></div>
<div class="text">
<div id="text-024a592a42" class="cmp-text">
    <p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">IT services segment revenue flat sequentially and increased 0.6% YoY CC</span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Operating Margin at 16.5% expanded 0.5% QoQ</span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">EPS increased 4.2% YoY; Operating cash flow at 165.8% of Net income</span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline"><b>EAST BRUNSWICK, N.J. | BENGALURU, India – October 15, 2026</b>: Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO), a leading AI-powered technology services and consulting company, announced financial results under International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS) for the quarter ended September 30, 2026.</span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-text-rgb-54-35-88 wpr-fs-32px wpr-display-inline"><u><b>Highlights of the Results</b></u></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline"><b>Results for the Quarter ended September 30, 2026:</b></span></p>
<ol><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Gross revenue at ₹247.5 billion ($2,583.0 million<sup>1</sup>), an increase of 1.1% QoQ and 9.1% YoY.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">IT services segment revenue was at $2611.5 million, decrease of 0.1% QoQ and increase of 0.3% YoY.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Non-GAAP constant currency<sup>2</sup> IT Services segment revenue was flat sequentially and increase of 0.6% YoY.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Total Bookings<sup>3</sup> was at $2,595 million, down by 22.9% QoQ in constant currency<sup>2</sup>. Large deal bookings<sup>4</sup> was at $674 million, decrease of 58.6% QoQ in constant currency<sup>2</sup>.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">IT services operating margin<sup>5</sup> for Q2’27 was at 16.5%, up by 0.5% QoQ and down by 0.2% YoY.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Net income for the quarter was at ₹32.0 billion ($333.9 million<sup>1</sup>), decrease of 4.7% QoQ and 1.9% YoY.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Earnings per share for the quarter at ₹3.23 ($0.03<sup>1</sup>), increase of 0.9% QoQ and increase of 4.2% YoY.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Operating cash flows of ₹53.0 billion ($553.6 million<sup>1</sup>), increase of 61.3% QoQ and at 165.8% of net income for the quarter.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Voluntary attrition was at 13.8% on a trailing 12-month basis.</span></li></ol>

</div>

    

</div>
<div class="text">
<div id="text-56fcf01b53" class="cmp-text">
    <p><span class="wpr-text-rgb-54-35-88 wpr-fs-32px wpr-display-inline"><u><b>Outlook for the Quarter ending December 31, 2026</b></u></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">We expect revenue from our IT Services business segment to be in the range of $2,571 million to $2,625 million*. This translates to sequential guidance of (-)1.5% to (&#43;)0.5% in constant currency terms.</span></p>
<p><i>*Outlook for the Quarter ending December 31, 2026, is based on the following exchange rates: GBP/USD at 1.35, Euro/USD at 1.15 , AUD/USD at 0.71, USD/INR at  95.76 and CAD/USD at 0.72</i></p>
<p><span class="wpr-text-rgb-54-35-88 wpr-fs-32px wpr-display-inline"><u><b>Performance for the Quarter ended September 30, 2026</b></u></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline"><b>Srini Pallia, CEO and Managing Director, said</b>, <i>“The strategic investments we have been making are beginning to deliver results. They are enhancing our ability to win in new markets, add new clients, and grow existing relationships. At the same time, our consulting-led, AI-powered strategy is helping us create larger transformation opportunities. We see AI as a long-term growth driver that will expand the addressable market for technology and business transformation. We are already seeing its potential reflected in the momentum across our AI-Native Unit and AI offerings portfolio”.</i></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline"><b>Aparna Iyer, Chief Financial Officer, said</b>, “Our operating margin for the quarter was 16.5%, an expansion of 0.5% sequentially. We have delivered this improvement even while continuing to invest in our business and people. We remain relentless in driving cash flow conversion. Q2 is yet another quarter where our operating cash flow has been robust and stood at 166% of net income.”</span></p>
<ol><li>For the convenience of the readers, the amounts in Indian Rupees in this release have been translated into United States Dollars at the certified foreign exchange rate of US$1 &#61; ₹95.83, as published by the Federal Reserve Board of Governors on September 30, 2026. However, the realized exchange rate in our IT Services business segment for the quarter ended September 30, 2026, was US$1&#61; ₹94.45</li><li>Constant currency (CC) for a period is the product of volumes in that period times the average actual exchange rate of the corresponding comparative period.</li><li>Total Bookings refers to the total contract value of all orders that were booked during the period including new orders, renewals, and increases to existing contracts. Bookings do not reflect subsequent terminations or reductions related to bookings originally recorded in prior fiscal periods. Bookings are recorded using then-existing foreign currency exchange rates and are not subsequently adjusted for foreign currency exchange rate fluctuations. The revenues from these contracts accrue over the tenure of the contract. For constant currency growth rates, refer note 2.</li><li>Large deal bookings consist of deals greater than or equal to $30 million in total contract value.</li><li>IT Services Operating Margin refers to Segment Results Total as reflected in IFRS financial.</li></ol>
<p><span class="wpr-text-rgb-54-35-88 wpr-fs-32px wpr-display-inline"><b><u>Highlights of Strategic Deal Wins</u></b></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">In Q2’27, Wipro continued to win large and strategic deals across industries. Key highlights include:</span></p>
<ol><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">One of the largest US-based banking institutions has selected Wipro to modernize its mortgage operations through Wipro&#39;s lending platform NetOxygen. Powered by Wipro Intelligence™, the platform will be implemented to simplify lending processes, automate key tasks, and provide actionable insights to support faster and more informed decision-making. Deployment of this platform is expected to improve borrower experience, accelerate loan closing times, and create a more efficient, scalable, and compliant lending ecosystem.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">A global technology company has renewed and expanded its relationship with Wipro to modernize its Enterprise Products organization and enhance employee experience through more resilient and scalable applications. As part of this multi-year engagement, Wipro will strengthen the client’s application landscape, support the development of AI-enabled enterprise solutions, and consolidate responsibilities into a unified delivery model. Wipro will leverage intelligent automation and AI-powered engineering capabilities to improve productivity, accelerate testing and delivery, and create a more integrated, cost-efficient operating model that enhances application reliability and user experience.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Seeking to improve operational efficiency and overall stakeholder experience, a leading US-based health insurance provider has appointed Wipro as a strategic partner to transform its provider services organization. Wipro will combine end-to-end provider support services with analytics, workforce planning, quality management, and operational excellence methodologies to identify root causes, optimize workflows, and improve business outcomes. This engagement will help accelerate issue resolution, enhance customer experience, and create a more scalable and cost-efficient operating model.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was selected by a global biotechnology company to transform and scale its post-market quality assurance operations to address changing regulatory requirements and the need for greater operational efficiency. Wipro will deliver end-to-end complaint management, reporting, and multilingual support services. Wipro will also introduce an AI-enabled operating model to ensure intelligent document processing, workflow orchestration, and automated compliance support. This transformation will improve processing speed, quality, and audit readiness, while reducing costs and creating a more resilient organization.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline"> A leading Asia-based Fortune 500 conglomerate selected Wipro to establish an AI Global Capability Center (GCC) as part of its enterprise AI transformation agenda. The engagement combines AI engineering talent, governance, innovation programs, and capability building to accelerate the development of AI-powered products and platforms while creating a scalable operating model for long-term growth.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">A leading global network technology provider has selected Wipro for a strategic engagement to scale its core mobile network services business worldwide. Wipro will provide network implementation, testing, and AI-led automation to simplify delivery and improve operational efficiency. The engagement will enable the client to expand delivery capacity, accelerate service deployment, and enhance quality and consistency across customer programs through a centralized delivery model.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">In a significant win for Wipro&#39;s AI-Native Business &amp; Platform unit, a large North American public services organization has selected Wipro to modernize its enrolment, customer engagement, and operational management processes. Wipro will deploy an AI-native digital operations platform designed to streamline onboarding, communications, and workflow management through a unified operating model. Powered by AI agents, conversational AI, intelligent document processing and predictive analytics, the platform will automate complex processes, enhance operational efficiency, and improve user experiences at scale. This win further demonstrates growing demand for AI-native platforms that help organizations simplify operations, improve service outcomes, and accelerate digital transformation.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">A global leader in beverages has awarded Wipro an expanded engagement to simplify, consolidate and optimize its technology operations. Wipro will deliver end-to-end infrastructure and hybrid cloud services, enhanced with Wipro Intelligence™, to provide personalized support, proactive issue resolution, automation of routine tasks, and improved operational visibility. The engagement will enhance employee experience, improve service performance, strengthen compliance, and cost optimization.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">A Europe-based global provider of industrial products and service solutions has renewed its engagement with Wipro for an enterprise-wide business transformation. Wipro will implement a single global enterprise resource planning platform, standardizing processes and data across regions while modernizing the client&#39;s core business systems. The program will provide real-time operational and financial visibility, improve efficiency, and enhance the agility needed to scale and respond more quickly to evolving market and customer demands.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">A leading global life sciences company has selected Wipro to establish an AI-powered supply chain intelligence platform to improve the speed, consistency, and quality of critical decisions. Beginning with a consulting-led assessment of business processes, data readiness, and governance requirements, Wipro will establish a trusted data foundation and deploy agents through WEGA to improve manufacturing, distribution, and inventory management decisions. This engagement will help accelerate decision-making, strengthen supplier risk visibility, improve responsiveness to supply disruptions, and create a scalable platform for future growth.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">A major energy company in the Middle East has selected Wipro to transform its procurement and finance operations through an AI-led operating model. Leveraging Wipro Intelligence™, Wipro will automate procurement workflows, supplier interactions, invoice management, and exception resolution. This will enable a more efficient, scalable and insight-driven enterprise operations function.</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">A leading North American financial services institution is modernizing its trade exception management capability with Capco, a Wipro company, to create a single view of trade, settlement, and position exceptions across the enterprise. Capco will design and implement a scalable platform that consolidates data from multiple internal and external sources, enabling faster investigation and resolution of operational exceptions. The solution will introduce AI-assisted exception detection, enhanced auditability, and configurable workflows to strengthen accountability, and operational controls.</span></li></ol>
<p><span class="wpr-text-rgb-54-35-88 wpr-fs-32px wpr-display-inline"><b><u>Analyst Recognitions</u></b></span></p>
<ol><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was recognized as a Leader in IDC MarketScape: Worldwide AI-Driven Professional Services for Oil and Gas Companies 2026 Vendor Assessment (Doc # US54135126 Aug 2026)</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was recognized as a Leader in ISG Provider Lens® - Microsoft AI and Cloud Ecosystem 2026 - US (all quadrants)</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was rated as a Leader in Avasant&#39;s Healthcare Payor Digital Services 2026 RadarView™</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was featured as a Leader in Avasant&#39;s Telecom Digital Services 2026 RadarView™</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was ranked as a Leader in Avasant&#39;s Utilities Digital Services 2026 RadarView™</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was positioned as a Leader in Everest Group&#39;s Cybersecurity Services PEAK Matrix® Assessment 2026 – Global</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was positioned as a Leader in IDC MarketScape: Worldwide Oracle Implementation Services 2026 Vendor Assessment (Doc # US54124626 Aug 2026)</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was positioned as a Leader in ISG Provider Lens® - Future of Work Services 2026 - US &amp; Europe (all quadrants)</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was recognized as a Leader in Everest Group&#39;s Quality Engineering (QE) Services for AI Applications and Systems PEAK Matrix® Assessment 2026</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was rated as a Leader in Everest Group&#39;s Application Management Services PEAK Matrix® Assessment 2026</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro was positioned as a Leader in Everest Group&#39;s Integrated Finance and Accounting Services (FAS) PEAK Matrix® Assessment 2026</span></li></ol>
<p><span class="wpr-text-rgb-54-35-88 wpr-fs-32px wpr-display-inline"><b><u>IT Products</u></b></span></p>
<ol><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">IT Products segment revenue for the quarter was ₹1.5 billion ($15.8 million<sup>1</sup>)</span></li><li><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">IT Products segment results for the quarter were (-) ₹0.1 billion ((-) $0.8 million<sup>1</sup>)</span></li></ol>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Please refer to the table on page 11 for reconciliation between IFRS IT Services Revenue and IT Services Revenue on a non-GAAP constant currency basis.</span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-text-rgb-54-35-88 wpr-fs-32px wpr-display-inline"><b><u>About Key Metrics and Non-GAAP Financial Measures</u></b></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">This press release contains key metrics and non-GAAP financial measures within the meaning of Regulation G and Item 10(e) of Regulation S-K. Such non-GAAP financial measures are measures of our historical or future performance, financial position or cash flows that are adjusted to exclude or include amounts that are excluded or included, as the case may be, from the most directly comparable financial measure calculated and presented in accordance with IFRS.</span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">The table on page 11 provides IT Services Revenue on a constant currency basis, which is a non-GAAP financial measure that is calculated by translating IT Services Revenue from the current reporting period into U.S. dollars based on the currency conversion rate in effect for the prior reporting period. We refer to growth rates in constant currency so that business results may be viewed without the impact of fluctuations in foreign currency exchange rates, thereby facilitating period-to-period comparisons of our business performance. Further, in the normal course of business, we may divest a portion of our business which may not be strategic. We refer to the growth rates in both reported and constant currency adjusting for such divestments in order to represent the comparable growth rates.</span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Our key metrics and non-GAAP financial measures are not based on any comprehensive set of accounting rules or principles and should not be considered a substitute for, or superior to, the most directly comparable financial measure calculated in accordance with IFRS and may be different from non-GAAP measures used by other companies. Our key metrics and non-GAAP financial measures are not comparable to, nor should be substituted for, an analysis of our revenue over time and involve estimates and judgments. In addition to our non-GAAP measures, the financial statements prepared in accordance with IFRS and the reconciliation of these non-GAAP financial measures with the most directly comparable IFRS financial measure should be carefully evaluated. </span></p>
<p><b><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Results for the Quarter ended September 30, 2026, prepared under IFRS, along with individual business segment reports, are available in the Investors section of our website <a href="/investors/">www.wipro.com/investors/</a></span></b></p>
<p><span class="wpr-text-rgb-54-35-88 wpr-fs-32px wpr-display-inline"><b>Quarterly Conference Call</b></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">We will hold an earnings conference call today at 07:00 p.m. Indian Standard Time (9:30 a.m. U.S. Eastern Time) to discuss our performance for the quarter. The audio from the conference call will be available online through a webcast and can be accessed at the following link-<a href="https://event.choruscall.com/mediaframe/webcast.html?webcastid&#61;0q8EorJM" rel="nofollow">https://event.choruscall.com/mediaframe/webcast.html?webcastid&#61;0q8EorJM</a></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">An audio recording of the management discussions and the question-and-answer session will be available online and will be accessible in the Investor Relations section of our website at <a href="/en/">www.wipro.com</a></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-text-rgb-54-35-88 wpr-fs-32px wpr-display-inline"><b>About Wipro Limited</b></span></p>
<p><span class="wpr-fs-20px wpr-display-inline">Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO) is a leading AI-powered technology services and consulting company focused on building innovative solutions that address clients’ most complex digital transformation needs. Leveraging our consulting-led approach and the Wipro Intelligence™ unified suite of AI-powered platforms, solutions and transformative offerings, we help clients realize their boldest ambitions to build intelligent and sustainable businesses. The Wipro Innovation Network – part of the Wipro Intelligence™ suite – underpins our commitment to client-centric co-innovation and co-creation by bringing together capabilities from the innovation labs and partner labs, academia, and global tech communities.  With over 230,000 employees and business partners across 65 countries, we deliver on the promise of helping our customers, colleagues, and communities thrive in an ever-changing world. For additional information, visit us at <a href="/en/">www.wipro.com</a>.</span></p>

</div>

    

</div>

        
